1
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:14,125
(Ryu Se-il)

2
00:00:20,333 --> 00:00:22,042
(Ha Jung-hoon)

3
00:00:27,792 --> 00:00:29,417
(Lee Jung-chan)

4
00:00:34,875 --> 00:00:36,625
(Jung Si-wan)

5
00:00:44,917 --> 00:00:46,708
"Boy, with Caution"

6
00:01:08,208 --> 00:01:09,458
Leave.

7
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:12,375
Let's pretend today never happened.

8
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:17,833
I don't want to.

9
00:01:21,375 --> 00:01:22,958
Did I do something wrong?

10
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:34,083
"Boy, with Caution"
(Episode 5)

11
00:02:38,611 --> 00:02:42,131
Didn't I tell you to stop dragging me into
things you can't even take responsibility for?

12
00:02:46,375 --> 00:02:47,848
Just let me look after a
student one more time.

13
00:02:47,872 --> 00:02:49,992
When will you saying "one
more time" even end for you?

14
00:02:51,938 --> 00:02:53,324
Just leave them be!

15
00:03:04,708 --> 00:03:07,458
There was a student in the
past I cared deeply about, too.

16
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:10,750
(2021)

17
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:18,208
Did you sleep here again?

18
00:03:21,750 --> 00:03:22,958
Get up.

19
00:03:38,667 --> 00:03:39,958
(6:20 AM)
Mr. Jang.

20
00:03:41,875 --> 00:03:44,542
You came in before 7:00?

21
00:03:45,542 --> 00:03:48,250
It's not because of me, is it?

22
00:03:57,792 --> 00:03:59,559
Why is it always the boreumdal
bread every single day?

23
00:03:59,583 --> 00:04:01,333
Don't they have the custard cream ones?

24
00:04:01,458 --> 00:04:02,917
When are you planning to go home?

25
00:04:06,125 --> 00:04:07,542
Whenever I change my mind.

26
00:04:09,458 --> 00:04:10,958
In that case...

27
00:04:11,083 --> 00:04:13,833
Go wash your uniform at the laundromat.

28
00:04:13,958 --> 00:04:16,917
Wear your gym clothes for class today.

29
00:04:17,583 --> 00:04:18,792
Why?

30
00:04:19,667 --> 00:04:22,292
Do I smell?

31
00:04:23,917 --> 00:04:25,208
A little.

32
00:04:30,792 --> 00:04:31,792
I'll go wash it.

33
00:04:37,583 --> 00:04:40,500
By the way, Mr. Jang,
keep an eye on my leftover bread.

34
00:04:40,625 --> 00:04:41,750
I'm having it for lunch.

35
00:04:47,375 --> 00:04:49,750
She never complained about her life.

36
00:04:49,875 --> 00:04:50,917
She always wore a smile.

37
00:04:51,375 --> 00:04:52,250
Did you guys hear?

38
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:53,042
Hear what?

39
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:54,559
She ran away from
home and sleeps at school.

40
00:04:54,583 --> 00:04:56,750
Look, she just wore her gym clothes today.

41
00:04:56,875 --> 00:04:58,875
Maybe she uses them as pajamas.

42
00:05:00,333 --> 00:05:03,417
Hey! I can hear everything.

43
00:05:04,417 --> 00:05:06,125
Besides, you guys don't know a thing.

44
00:05:06,250 --> 00:05:07,833
These aren't pajamas.

45
00:05:08,792 --> 00:05:10,333
I always sleep in my uniform!

46
00:05:14,750 --> 00:05:16,000
Jung Soo-bin.

47
00:05:18,667 --> 00:05:21,000
Only I knew it was all just an act.

48
00:05:26,792 --> 00:05:28,708
Yet even so, I still pushed her away.

49
00:05:30,875 --> 00:05:31,958
Soo-bin.

50
00:05:35,250 --> 00:05:36,875
I spoke with your mother on the phone.

51
00:05:40,833 --> 00:05:41,667
Go home after you finish eating.

52
00:05:41,792 --> 00:05:43,432
I already excused your absence for today.

53
00:05:46,625 --> 00:05:47,750
I don't want to.

54
00:05:50,792 --> 00:05:52,809
If you think I'm such a nuisance,
then just leave me alone.

55
00:05:52,833 --> 00:05:54,125
I'll take care of myself.

56
00:05:55,375 --> 00:05:56,708
That's not what I mean.

57
00:05:56,833 --> 00:05:58,167
Then what is it?

58
00:05:59,708 --> 00:06:01,542
Are you going to look
out for me all the way?

59
00:06:02,375 --> 00:06:03,393
You can't even do that yourself.

60
00:06:03,417 --> 00:06:05,417
That's why you're telling
me to compromise, right?

61
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:10,458
Neither here nor there.

62
00:06:11,167 --> 00:06:12,708
My dad used to say...

63
00:06:12,833 --> 00:06:15,667
the hardest thing is doing just enough
without standing out.

64
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:19,125
That's why it's so dull.

65
00:06:20,292 --> 00:06:22,375
Everyone lives such dull lives.

66
00:06:24,375 --> 00:06:26,750
Looking at you, Mr. Jang,
I finally get what he meant.

67
00:06:32,083 --> 00:06:33,625
Go home once you finish eating.

68
00:06:34,875 --> 00:06:36,125
Don't come to class today.

69
00:06:52,417 --> 00:06:55,292
Off campus, in private...

70
00:06:56,792 --> 00:06:59,000
you met with student
Jung Soo-bin, didn't you?

71
00:07:01,583 --> 00:07:03,042
Mr. Jang Gi-woo.

72
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,125
Your silence...

73
00:07:07,083 --> 00:07:09,250
does that mean you admit it?

74
00:07:12,042 --> 00:07:14,208
Soo-bin is going through a tough time,

75
00:07:14,333 --> 00:07:16,292
so I did speak with her in private.

76
00:07:16,917 --> 00:07:19,000
But those rumors...

77
00:07:19,125 --> 00:07:20,667
It's not like that at all.

78
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,958
I had to talk to her about
her situation at home.

79
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,125
It was about her staying at school, right?

80
00:07:29,292 --> 00:07:29,917
Yes.

81
00:07:30,042 --> 00:07:31,917
It couldn't be helped.

82
00:07:33,750 --> 00:07:35,792
I was the one who pushed her away,

83
00:07:35,917 --> 00:07:37,101
yet I acted like I knew nothing.

84
00:07:37,125 --> 00:07:38,292
Right.

85
00:07:44,708 --> 00:07:46,458
It was all because of me,

86
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:49,190
yet I only thought of saving myself.

87
00:07:49,875 --> 00:07:51,125
Ms. Kim So-jung.

88
00:07:51,250 --> 00:07:51,833
Yes?

89
00:07:51,958 --> 00:07:53,278
Could you come here for a moment?

90
00:07:58,500 --> 00:08:00,000
If Jung Soo-bin is in class,

91
00:08:00,125 --> 00:08:01,833
please have her come by.

92
00:08:01,958 --> 00:08:06,125
Well, Soo-bin submitted a withdrawal form.

93
00:08:22,458 --> 00:08:24,250
This is because of me too, isn't it?

94
00:08:28,292 --> 00:08:30,542
You're really overthinking this.

95
00:08:32,750 --> 00:08:34,583
I truly don't get it.

96
00:08:41,167 --> 00:08:43,458
How can having feelings
for someone be wrong?

97
00:08:57,583 --> 00:09:00,000
Is all you feel really just
remorse over a mistake?

98
00:09:10,375 --> 00:09:13,250
Did your feelings ever waver,

99
00:09:14,208 --> 00:09:15,708
even for a single second?

100
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,417
That's what I'm curious about.

101
00:09:30,167 --> 00:09:31,750
Think whatever you want.

102
00:09:34,750 --> 00:09:36,250
Can I really?

103
00:09:41,458 --> 00:09:43,125
It's all just in your head anyway.

104
00:09:57,167 --> 00:09:59,143
(Regret: I have never wavered.)
I have never wavered.

105
00:09:59,167 --> 00:10:00,958
Nor have I ever been shaken up.

106
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,083
Then let's start now.

107
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:25,792
I'll do it myself.

108
00:10:27,583 --> 00:10:29,543
If I have to say it twice,
you're getting beaten.

109
00:10:36,625 --> 00:10:37,792
Take it off.

110
00:10:38,333 --> 00:10:39,853
You look to pretty in it, it won't do.

111
00:10:41,042 --> 00:10:42,500
You're not one of us.

112
00:10:45,458 --> 00:10:47,083
Cheap clothes suit you better.

113
00:10:56,500 --> 00:10:57,750
Hey, Vending Machine.

114
00:10:59,792 --> 00:11:01,952
Are you gonna punch me if
you have to call twice, too?

115
00:11:02,042 --> 00:11:02,833
I was just about to.

116
00:11:02,958 --> 00:11:04,208
Okay.

117
00:11:05,333 --> 00:11:07,518
The collateral we got from that loser today
is worth twelve million won.

118
00:11:07,542 --> 00:11:09,462
You wanted to borrow
ten million from me, right?

119
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,042
And so?

120
00:11:16,125 --> 00:11:18,565
If I sold you right now,
would you [be worth] ten million won?

121
00:11:24,042 --> 00:11:26,583
Get your act together and
make the delivery properly.

122
00:11:32,583 --> 00:11:33,833
Otherwise...

123
00:11:35,625 --> 00:11:38,042
you might lose this hand, too.

124
00:11:40,417 --> 00:11:41,792
Deal?

125
00:11:44,292 --> 00:11:45,708
It's a deal.

126
00:11:53,542 --> 00:11:55,102
Cram school should be letting out soon.

127
00:11:58,250 --> 00:11:59,542
Hey, Vending Machine.

128
00:12:04,750 --> 00:12:06,833
If you go soft, you're dead meat.

129
00:12:23,458 --> 00:12:24,667
Kim Jeong-ha.

130
00:12:28,042 --> 00:12:29,708
You're here for the collateral, right?

131
00:12:30,917 --> 00:12:32,750
Did you decide to work for them?

132
00:12:33,208 --> 00:12:34,542
None of your business.

133
00:12:48,292 --> 00:12:49,292
It's not a fake, is it?

134
00:12:49,375 --> 00:12:51,055
The certificate of authenticity is inside.

135
00:12:51,583 --> 00:12:54,103
I looked it up. It originally
retailed for fifteen million won.

136
00:12:58,042 --> 00:12:59,542
When are you wiring the money?

137
00:13:03,042 --> 00:13:04,962
You're borrowing money
to buy drugs, aren't you?

138
00:13:07,625 --> 00:13:09,417
Quit while you still can.

139
00:13:09,542 --> 00:13:11,125
I asked when you're wiring the money.

140
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:14,708
Once it's verified, it'll be wired today.

141
00:13:15,333 --> 00:13:17,583
The deadline to repay
is one week, as agreed.

142
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,375
With twenty percent interest.

143
00:13:25,958 --> 00:13:27,208
My mom's here.

144
00:13:28,542 --> 00:13:30,042
Make sure you wire it today.

145
00:13:37,917 --> 00:13:39,250
Let's have a talk.

146
00:13:41,292 --> 00:13:42,708
I'm busy right now.

147
00:13:42,833 --> 00:13:44,273
Because of your part-time job again?

148
00:13:45,708 --> 00:13:46,917
Some other time.

149
00:14:02,083 --> 00:14:03,667
Pretty nice. Just my style.

150
00:14:04,375 --> 00:14:05,667
I'll wire the money.

151
00:14:07,833 --> 00:14:09,958
Hey, someone at your
school is dealing drugs too?

152
00:14:10,833 --> 00:14:12,434
That shut-in didn't look like
the type to do drugs, though.

153
00:14:12,458 --> 00:14:14,125
Wonder how he got hooked on it.

154
00:14:14,625 --> 00:14:15,792
Interesting.

155
00:14:16,042 --> 00:14:17,208
Yeah, there is.

156
00:14:18,250 --> 00:14:19,500
What's their name?

157
00:14:21,958 --> 00:14:24,893
I got expelled for dealing back then.
Still leaves a bad taste in my mouth.

158
00:14:24,917 --> 00:14:26,083
Lee Hyeon-jae.

159
00:14:35,958 --> 00:14:37,167
Lee Hyeon-jae?

160
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:41,833
It's been a while.

161
00:14:43,708 --> 00:14:44,917
He's still in school?

162
00:14:46,875 --> 00:14:48,000
Yeah.

163
00:14:53,417 --> 00:14:54,542
Vending Machine.

164
00:14:55,417 --> 00:14:57,657
Right, you said you'd hit
me if I called you that again.

165
00:14:58,375 --> 00:14:59,458
Jeong-ha.

166
00:15:00,458 --> 00:15:01,667
Go to school.

167
00:15:02,792 --> 00:15:05,250
Stop running errands and
collecting debts gig by gig.

168
00:15:05,375 --> 00:15:06,815
All we need is to get Lee Hyeon-jae.

169
00:15:08,542 --> 00:15:09,976
Just bring me Lee Hyeon-jae's phone,

170
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,840
and I'll give you ten
million won in one shot.

171
00:15:18,917 --> 00:15:20,708
What's there to hesitate about?

172
00:15:22,708 --> 00:15:24,292
Or do you have cold feet?

173
00:15:39,542 --> 00:15:40,708
Okay.

174
00:15:41,417 --> 00:15:42,777
Lee Hyeon-jae did this, didn't he?

175
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:45,042
So that's your reason.

176
00:15:52,958 --> 00:15:54,125
Bring it tomorrow.

177
00:15:56,375 --> 00:15:57,708
Ten million won.

178
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:00,208
Don't forget.

179
00:16:17,208 --> 00:16:18,875
Has anyone heard from Jeong-ha?

180
00:16:38,333 --> 00:16:39,667
Why are you late?

181
00:16:40,833 --> 00:16:42,375
I had to go to the hospital.

182
00:16:44,083 --> 00:16:45,292
I'm sorry.

183
00:16:48,417 --> 00:16:49,857
That's all for the morning assembly.

184
00:17:22,875 --> 00:17:24,208
What is it?

185
00:17:27,708 --> 00:17:28,708
Something on your mind?

186
00:17:30,833 --> 00:17:33,542
What time is counseling today?

187
00:17:37,750 --> 00:17:39,167
I was worried you forgot.

188
00:17:45,208 --> 00:17:46,708
Where should we begin?

189
00:17:49,333 --> 00:17:50,833
Right from that incident.

190
00:18:00,917 --> 00:18:02,250
Did you do that on purpose?

191
00:18:09,458 --> 00:18:12,042
Otherwise, you'd just
pretend it never happened.

192
00:18:15,667 --> 00:18:18,726
Didn't you tell me that you shouldn't
pretend nothing happened when there is,

193
00:18:18,750 --> 00:18:20,270
even if you don't have the confidence?

194
00:18:29,917 --> 00:18:32,877
If you don't want a professional counselor,
then we'll cancel the sessions.

195
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:33,833
Mr. Jang.

196
00:18:33,958 --> 00:18:35,167
We'll call it off for today.

197
00:18:35,292 --> 00:18:37,542
Ms. Lee Ga-eun will take over next week.

198
00:18:37,667 --> 00:18:38,458
You two have met before, right?

199
00:18:38,583 --> 00:18:39,375
Mr. Jang.

200
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:42,375
Do you still want to continue counseling?

201
00:18:47,250 --> 00:18:48,458
No need.

202
00:18:49,417 --> 00:18:50,792
Let's leave it at that, then.

203
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:54,500
Is that all?

204
00:19:08,708 --> 00:19:10,542
Because I don't have the confidence either—

205
00:19:13,375 --> 00:19:15,375
pretending nothing
happened when it clearly did.

206
00:19:20,583 --> 00:19:22,833
If I gave you the wrong
impression, I'm sorry.

207
00:19:23,583 --> 00:19:25,863
But I'd appreciate it if you
never brought this up again.

208
00:19:32,417 --> 00:19:35,000
I'd never get the wrong
impression of someone "dull."

209
00:19:42,042 --> 00:19:45,417
I've been wanting to
tell you this all along.

210
00:19:50,250 --> 00:19:51,542
You can leave now.

211
00:20:45,125 --> 00:20:46,485
Give me the ten million won first.

212
00:20:47,458 --> 00:20:49,542
You really know how
to look out for yourself.

213
00:20:50,083 --> 00:20:53,000
You really are my type.

214
00:20:57,208 --> 00:20:58,848
(10,000,000 KRW Transferred Successfully)

215
00:21:05,875 --> 00:21:08,083
Does this guy have no friends?

216
00:21:08,208 --> 00:21:13,083
Dad, Mom, Secretary, Mr. Jang Gi-woo.

217
00:21:25,083 --> 00:21:27,833
What do you think feelings are?

218
00:21:27,958 --> 00:21:29,375
When do you feel them?

219
00:21:32,542 --> 00:21:34,125
Found it. Something interesting.

220
00:21:55,667 --> 00:21:56,833
Was it you?

221
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:59,125
What?

222
00:21:59,667 --> 00:22:00,875
My phone.

223
00:22:01,708 --> 00:22:03,708
Why are you asking me for your phone?

224
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:06,375
Didn't you even send someone to beat me up?

225
00:22:07,125 --> 00:22:10,500
That guy, Vending Machine Kim Jeong-ha.

226
00:22:10,875 --> 00:22:12,208
Kim Jeong-ha said that?

227
00:22:18,583 --> 00:22:19,917
Answer me.

228
00:22:21,917 --> 00:22:23,208
Where's my phone?

229
00:22:23,333 --> 00:22:25,417
I really don't know! It wasn't me!

230
00:22:25,542 --> 00:22:27,917
Why would I even steal your phone?

231
00:22:46,667 --> 00:22:47,917
Where is Kim Jeong-ha?

232
00:22:54,583 --> 00:22:56,042
Oh, dear.

233
00:22:57,917 --> 00:22:59,792
A nursing hospital
must be really expensive.

234
00:22:59,917 --> 00:23:02,417
Where did you get the
money to pay for this?

235
00:23:03,833 --> 00:23:05,083
I don't have money,

236
00:23:05,208 --> 00:23:07,083
but the government does.

237
00:23:07,208 --> 00:23:09,583
Since you stayed here so
long, there must be a lot to pack.

238
00:23:09,917 --> 00:23:11,833
You have to transfer next week.

239
00:23:12,917 --> 00:23:14,375
The government covers it?

240
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:15,667
Of course.

241
00:23:17,625 --> 00:23:18,292
Have a piece.

242
00:23:18,417 --> 00:23:21,292
No, my teeth are too sensitive.

243
00:23:21,417 --> 00:23:24,083
Come on, it's really sweet.

244
00:23:31,458 --> 00:23:32,583
Get out.

245
00:23:33,583 --> 00:23:35,125
Let's talk outside first.

246
00:23:36,167 --> 00:23:39,125
Is that your friend? Come
have some watermelon!

247
00:23:40,542 --> 00:23:42,750
Please, let's just go outside. Please.

248
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:48,167
It was you, right?

249
00:23:50,583 --> 00:23:51,750
Kim Ji Tae.

250
00:23:52,875 --> 00:23:54,542
Kim Ji Tae made me do it.

251
00:23:55,750 --> 00:23:58,333
The moment he heard your name,
he told me to steal your phone.

252
00:24:01,667 --> 00:24:03,458
My grandma doesn't
know anything about this.

253
00:24:04,625 --> 00:24:06,708
- Please, just go outside.
- Is he at the pool hall?

254
00:24:15,542 --> 00:24:16,750
Grandma.

255
00:24:19,875 --> 00:24:21,042
Did you know?

256
00:24:26,750 --> 00:24:29,125
Watermelon tastes better
at room temperature.

257
00:24:49,333 --> 00:24:51,667
Your friend is so polite.

258
00:24:54,208 --> 00:24:55,583
He's not my friend.

259
00:25:07,068 --> 00:25:08,435
Mr. Regret, should we meet up?

260
00:25:10,482 --> 00:25:12,362
I think it's time for us
to meet face to face.

261
00:25:15,502 --> 00:25:16,502
Not gonna answer?

262
00:25:18,435 --> 00:25:19,435
Thinking about it?

263
00:25:32,708 --> 00:25:34,250
Where is Kim Ji Tae?

264
00:25:34,375 --> 00:25:35,375
Who the hell are you?

265
00:25:35,458 --> 00:25:36,458
I asked where he is.

266
00:25:36,583 --> 00:25:39,083
I asked who you are, idiot. Are you deaf?

267
00:25:39,458 --> 00:25:40,833
Call your boss and ask.

268
00:25:40,958 --> 00:25:42,998
Let's see how long you can
keep running that mouth.

269
00:25:46,958 --> 00:25:48,250
Agh!

270
00:25:52,042 --> 00:25:53,250
He just stepped out!

271
00:25:57,125 --> 00:25:57,875
Where?

272
00:25:58,000 --> 00:25:59,417
He said he was meeting someone.

273
00:25:59,542 --> 00:26:00,375
Who?

274
00:26:00,500 --> 00:26:02,125
Someone from a random chat app, I think.

275
00:26:02,250 --> 00:26:04,250
He's the one who stole the phone.

276
00:26:04,375 --> 00:26:06,042
He said there was something juicy on it.

277
00:26:06,625 --> 00:26:09,250
You know the one.
They advertise it on buses all the time.

278
00:26:09,375 --> 00:26:10,625
Amuna.

279
00:26:18,167 --> 00:26:19,417
Amuna?

280
00:26:33,042 --> 00:26:34,458
You're Regret, right?

281
00:26:36,792 --> 00:26:37,833
Yeah.

282
00:26:48,667 --> 00:26:50,000
Hello.

283
00:27:09,792 --> 00:27:11,125
"Boy, with Caution"

284
00:27:11,625 --> 00:27:13,393
(Next Episode Preview)
I want to keep seeing you.

285
00:27:13,417 --> 00:27:15,125
What should I call you?

286
00:27:15,250 --> 00:27:16,292
What did you say to him?

287
00:27:16,417 --> 00:27:17,726
Is Jang Gi-woo really that important?

288
00:27:17,750 --> 00:27:20,500
What on earth is he doing right now?

289
00:27:22,708 --> 00:27:24,125
So you really are here.

290
00:27:24,792 --> 00:27:25,875
Lee Hyeon-jae.

291
00:27:26,250 --> 00:27:29,042
I only did it because I liked you.

292
00:27:29,167 --> 00:27:32,875
What will it take for you to stop?

293
00:27:34,667 --> 00:27:37,917
Congratulations. You finally have
something you're afraid to lose.

294
00:27:38,292 --> 00:27:40,083
That guy's always been kind of gloomy.

295
00:27:40,667 --> 00:27:42,267
Is it because he grew up getting beaten?
